{
  "program": "CBTRN03C",
  "caseId": "case14",
  "description": "A negative amount through the detail mask. TRAN-REPORT-AMT is PIC -ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ.ZZ, whose leading minus is a fixed insertion character: it prints '-' for a negative value and a space for any other, so the sign occupies position 1 of the fifteen and never floats. Zero suppression replaces the leading zeros - and the comma that lies inside the suppressed run - with spaces and stops at the first significant digit, so 1234.56 negative renders as the exact string '-  1,234.56' with the mask's own geometry intact. The stored TRAN-AMT is a zoned S9(09)V99 whose sign is an overpunch in its trailing byte, which is what the DISPLAY lines at :198-199 show, and the page and grand totals go negative with it - through the + mask, where a negative value still prints '-'.",
